--- body ---
## Context

Reported from JETP-observer, 2026-11-09, after its ID-claims migration (its PR
#285). On every commit that stages a `.erg` file, the managed pre-commit block
runs `tickets/erg check tickets/`, which prints every corpus WARN: 236 in that
repo, mostly "log entry after the entry run's terminal blank". That is about
40 KB of output per ticket commit, enough to swamp an agent's tool output and
bury the one line that matters (ERG CHECK: PASS/FAIL).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The managed pre-commit block shows errors in full but WARNs only as a count (or only when `check` fails)
- [ ] `erg check` run by hand keeps its full output
- [ ] A test pins the hook's quiet output on a corpus with warnings and its full output on a failing one

## Notes

The hook block is written at install time: a repo that already has it keeps
the noisy version until `erg install --hooks` is run again. The fix should say
so where adopters will see it (release notes, or the install output).

## Imagine (raid f314e3)

Premise holds on main d364f2d: `hookBody` (src/go/install.go:102-105) runs
`tickets/erg check tickets/` uncaptured; WARNs go to stderr, the
`ERG CHECK: PASS (N tickets, M warnings)` line last on stdout.

Path: change the hook's shell only, no new `check` flag. `install --hooks`
rewrites the hook but never the vendored `tickets/erg`, and `cmdCheck` exits 1
on an unknown flag, so a hook calling a new flag would fail every ticket commit
where the vendored binary predates it. Capture check's combined output; on
failure print it all, on pass print only the `^ERG CHECK` line (grep, not
`tail -n 1`: on the empty-corpus path a WARN can come last). `erg check` by
hand is untouched, which meets criterion 2 by construction.

Change together: `hookBody`; its verbatim copy in src/go/assets/integration.md
(byte-compared by tests/test_selfcoherence.sh (iv)); tests in tests/test_hook.sh.

Blind spot 1 (decided: count only). The asset-drift WARN/NOTE lines
(check.go:280, manifest.go:606/672/734) are the upgrade nudge that
integration.md:248 promises ("`erg check` warns until it runs"); pre-commit is
where adopters see it unasked. Count-only buries it. Kept count-only because it
is criterion 1's letter; reword integration.md:248 so it does not imply the
commit shows it. Letting drift lines through is a scope change left to the
author.

Blind spot 2 (test design). Warnings print indented two spaces in four
spellings (`WARN x:`, `WARN:`, `WARNING:`, `NOTE`), so `^WARN ` cannot fail.
The fixture must carry a real warning (a fresh store passes clean); assert no
line matches `WARN|NOTE` and the PASS line reports N warnings; prove it red on
the current hook first.

Out of scope: this repo's 264 log-placement WARNs (a separate cleanup); the
per-file `erg validate` output (bounded by staged files).

## Plan (raid f314e3)

Actions:
1. src/go/install.go:99-102, inside `hookBody`: replace the `check` block with
   ```
   if ! erg_check_out=$(tickets/erg check tickets/ 2>&1); then
       printf '%s\n' "$erg_check_out" >&2
       echo "ERROR: ticket corpus check failed." >&2
       exit 1
   fi
   printf '%s\n' "$erg_check_out" | grep '^ERG CHECK' || true
   ```
   plus a one-line comment. No `exit 0`; `claimsIndexCheck` untouched.
2. src/go/assets/integration.md:47-50: the same lines, byte-identical
   (test_selfcoherence.sh (iv) compares them).
3. integration.md:247-248: "`erg check` run by hand warns until it runs, the
   pre-commit hook shows only a warning count" (no date, no ticket number:
   test_integration.sh:206-215).

First test (tests/test_hook.sh, new Tests 7-8 after Test 6, written first):
- Fixture: commit with `--no-verify` two warning carriers (0010, 0011), each with
  a blank line inside the header block (`WARN ...: blank line inside header
  block`). Not a stale Blocked-by: the hook's `erg validate` rejects it.
- Test 7, quiet pass: stage only a clean 0012 (+ claim), commit through the
  hook capturing `2>&1`; assert rc 0, no line matching unanchored
  case-sensitive `WARN|NOTE`, and `ERG CHECK: PASS (` with `2 warnings)`.
  Red on the current hook.
- Test 8, failing corpus: stage a closed-unarchived 0013 (+ claim); assert rc
  non-zero, HEAD unmoved, output holds `VIOLATION`, `closed ticket not in
  closed/ directory`, and both carriers' `WARN` lines. Green on the current
  hook too: a regression guard against an always-count-only fix, not a red test.

Untouched: test_install.sh:422-445 ratchets; integration.md is not a deployed
asset (no regen step). Optional dogfood: `build/erg install . --hooks`.
Expected diff: ~75 lines over 3 files.

## Feasibility (raid f314e3): PASS

Paths and lines checked on d364f2d (install.go:99-102, integration.md:47-50 and
246-248, test_selfcoherence.sh:106, test_hook.sh Test 6 at ~105,
`ERG="${ERG_BIN:-build/erg}"`). No open PR touches these files; single-ticket
wave, no shared registry.
